CODEGEN.md §5.2, §3.5; log-2026-09-24 "ir plans review": gen/cpp writes the enum helpers ToName and ToWire in the namespace, so a record ToWire next to an enum collides there (g++ refuses the header).
-- a/a.canon --
package a

/// A tone.
enum Tone { soft, loud }

/// A wire.
record ToWire {
  /// Its tone.
  tone: Tone
}

/// The wire.
let wire: ToWire = { tone: soft }

emit cpp { out: "@features/a", namespace: "a", mode: data }
emit json { out: "out/" }
